// Title: Potential Persistence Via Shim Database In Uncommon Location
// Sigma ID: 6b6976a3-b0e6-4723-ac24-ae38a737af41
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-08-01 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1546.011
// Description: Detects the installation of a new shim database where the file is located in a non-default
//   location
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/05/fin7-shim-databases-persistence.html
//   - https://andreafortuna.org/2018/11/12/process-injection-and-persistence-using-application-shimming/
//   - https://www.blackhat.com/docs/asia-14/materials/Erickson/Asia-14-Erickson-Persist-It-Using-And-Abusing-Microsofts-Fix-It-Patches.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_shim_database_uncommon_location.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\AppCompatFlags\\InstalledSDB.*$" and RegistryKey contains "\\DatabasePath") and (not(RegistryValueData contains ":\\Windows\\AppPatch\\Custom"))
